{"id":"b0751886a5bc31d33382a6440990138d7d218d6f366f82942799ccd390859b16","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:21:42.872079422Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nSub-issue of 215ee3.\n\n## What to build\n\nA Sync never drops a local operation, comment or link that has not yet been pushed, and never resurrects a deleted ticket. The pull's self-heal for a Stranded index no longer drops the local serialization ref and fast-forwards the remote over the store. Instead it computes remote ticket ids missing from the index (deleted tickets are indexed, so they never qualify), takes only those tickets' keys from the remote tracking tree, applies them to the store additively, then serializes fully so the local ref carries them. Tickets already indexed are never touched. The push's implicit-deletion guard is unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] CLI regression from the incident: two clones synced; in A add a comment on a ticket that already has remote comments, create two sub-issues of a map ticket, add dependencies, delete two tickets; `ti sync` in A against a remote holding the previous state; A keeps every comment, link and dependency; deleted stay deleted; B after sync sees all of it and hides the deleted tickets\n- [ ] Stranded-index self-heal still works: a clone whose index is missing remote tickets gains them on pull without losing its own unsynced edits\n- [ ] Existing race-window and sync reporting tests green\n- [ ] Local serialization ref is never deleted by pull (asserted through behaviour: unsynced work survives, not through ref inspection)"}}}